      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The FLN emerged in 1954 to organize a mass resistance campaign against French colonial rule, leading to the embassy bombings that sparked the official 1954 war. Throughout the 1950s and 1960s, the struggle became a \"people's war\" that included guerrilla operations, the \"inconnus\" (unknown fighters) who hid in the mountains to resist colonial infiltration, and the mobilization of unlisted people to defend their land. After the FLN's decisive victory in 1962, the struggle ended with the 1962 Accords and Algeria's full independence, cementing the narrative that the liberation was achieved by the will of the local population.",
